00:21:47.990 --> 00:21:49.890
Technical term.
I have pain there

00:21:51.090 --> 00:21:54.741
and so, I learned to sleep on my back

00:21:54.741 --> 00:21:57.907
and I can't spoon anymore
but the solution could be

00:21:57.907 --> 00:22:00.230
wear down the left shoulder.
You can spoon.

00:22:00.230 --> 00:22:01.790
I could get spooned.
You could spoon,

00:22:01.790 --> 00:22:05.460
but you can't spoon asleep,
but you can spoon just for fun.

00:22:05.460 --> 00:22:07.410
It still hurts.

00:22:07.410 --> 00:22:09.500
Or I think it's hurting.
There's no spooning now?

00:22:09.500 --> 00:22:13.290
I think, I can't spoon because I think

00:22:13.290 --> 00:22:16.070
that I'm grinding my shoulder
and so I actually try

00:22:16.070 --> 00:22:20.410
to keep my elbow down by
my hip and spoon that way.

00:22:20.410 --> 00:22:21.960
The thing about me--
And that's just weird.

00:22:21.960 --> 00:22:23.626
The thing about spooning for me--

00:22:23.626 --> 00:22:24.910
It's like you're upright
but you're laying down.

00:22:24.910 --> 00:22:27.210
Is I've always only
ever been the big spoon

00:22:27.210 --> 00:22:29.140
because if I'm the
little spoon with Jessie,

00:22:29.140 --> 00:22:31.240
it's like I have a backpack
on, you know what I'm saying?

00:22:31.240 --> 00:22:33.680
It's just not the same sensation.

00:22:33.680 --> 00:22:36.023
You're an ultra large little spoon.

00:22:38.730 --> 00:22:42.560
Shall we move on?
I just wanna make sure

00:22:42.560 --> 00:22:44.590
we got closure here.
We've told him he needs

00:22:44.590 --> 00:22:46.483
to talk to his wife about
this but then take it

00:22:46.483 --> 00:22:47.900
as an opportunity.
Ironically,

00:22:47.900 --> 00:22:49.600
you know what I'm gonna do tonight?

00:22:49.600 --> 00:22:52.180
I'm gonna get in bed
first, I'm gonna get in

00:22:52.180 --> 00:22:54.401
on Christy's side and I'm
not gonna say anything.

00:22:54.401 --> 00:22:55.234
Yeah that's not gonna work.

00:22:55.234 --> 00:22:56.067
I'm gonna go all the way to sleep

00:22:56.067 --> 00:22:56.900
and then see if she wakes me up.

00:22:56.900 --> 00:22:58.670
If you move the furniture it might work.

00:22:58.670 --> 00:23:00.737
Move all the stuff in there.
Yeah.

00:23:00.737 --> 00:23:04.810
I think Christy and I, all
right I'm audible here.

00:23:04.810 --> 00:23:09.810
Maybe we need to throw it
in the mix to switch it up.

00:23:09.850 --> 00:23:10.830
Yeah, see how it feels.

00:23:10.830 --> 00:23:12.900
Let's both, let's both
do that with our wives

00:23:12.900 --> 00:23:14.723
and then report back.

00:23:16.300 --> 00:23:19.050
Let's talk 'em, Jessie,
she won't care, right?

00:23:19.050 --> 00:23:21.390
Mm, I don't know, I gotta
talk to her about this.

00:23:21.390 --> 00:23:23.809
We can't decide right now for 'em.

00:23:23.809 --> 00:23:24.642
Listen if I've learned anything,

00:23:24.642 --> 00:23:26.577
I'm not gonna make a decision on a podcast

00:23:26.577 --> 00:23:29.943
that affects my wife.

00:23:29.943 --> 00:23:33.090
We're gonna begin
negotiations which may lead

00:23:33.090 --> 00:23:35.530
to a trial period of sleeping
on other side of the bed

00:23:35.530 --> 00:23:37.230
and see what happens.
Yeah, mix it up.

00:23:37.230 --> 00:23:40.299
But I guarantee you there'll
be some bad nights' sleep.

00:23:40.299 --> 00:23:41.920
Not for me.

00:23:41.920 --> 00:23:43.560
No I'm being honest with you.

00:23:43.560 --> 00:23:45.950
I know for a fact it's
not going to affect,

00:23:45.950 --> 00:23:49.375
'cause I do it randomly when
we travel and it's never--

00:23:49.375 --> 00:23:50.670
Thanks Mike for--

00:23:50.670 --> 00:23:54.040
So we got more questions but
first we wanna let you know

00:23:54.040 --> 00:23:56.710
that you can go to Mythical.com
